How does the CS2023 SE-Validation unit distinguish verification from validation?

Use these exact pinned knowledge graph excerpts and say what they do not prove:
{"claim":{"id":"se:CLM-TVV-0001","statement":"CS2023's SE-Validation unit defines verification and validation as two distinct questions — verification asks whether the thing is being built right, and validation asks whether the right thing was built — and its learning outcomes expect students to distinguish program validation from verification.","scope":"CS2023 SE-Validation knowledge unit, CS Core topic 1 and CS Core learning outcome 2.","limitations":"The two-question formulation distinguishes conformance-checking from fitness-for-purpose; it does not imply that passing tests proves correctness or that validation equals acceptance."},"evidence":{"id":"se:EVD-TVV-0003","statement":"CS Core topic 1 of the SE-Validation unit distinguishes verification (\"Are we building the thing right?\") from validation (\"Did we build the right thing?\"); illustrative learning outcome 2 expects students to distinguish between program validation and verification.","limitations":"The two-question formulation is a curriculum teaching device; the source does not elaborate when each question is fully answered."},"locator":{"id":"se:LOC-CS2023-SE-VALIDATION-KU","section":"Body of Knowledge, Software Engineering (SE), knowledge unit 'SE-Validation: Software Verification and Validation' (CS Core topics 1-5, KA Core topics 6-9, Non-core topics 10-14); heading and topic text verified by full-text extraction of the official PDF on 2026-11-06; printed page not independently confirmed, page anchor per registry: SE section spans PDF page indices 174-176"},"source":{"id":"se:SRC-CS2023","title":"Computer Science Curricula 2023","limitations":["Curriculum framework, not a complete professional Software Engineering domain taxonomy","Knowledge-unit counts do not establish professional-domain completeness"]}}
